[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The view check: the rules a tree of narratives must satisfy that strictdoc does not check

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-VIEW-CHECK
TITLE: The view check: the rules a tree of narratives must satisfy that strictdoc does not check
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
view-check.py --root UID walks the tree and reports, count first, exit 1
on any finding: Contains forms a tree (each narrative contained at most
once, no cycle -- strictdoc exits 0 on one); a Contains target is a
NARRATIVE; every row bracket word is in the root's legend; a narrative's
WIDGET agrees with its STATEMENT (rows has "- " items, glossary rows split
on the first ": ", legend rows on two, table rows on pipes); a cited node
is not superseded (a query, per DEC-SUPERSESSION-RULE); no node outside the
representation family points a Parent at a narrative in the tree. What
strictdoc already refuses -- a dangling Cites, a dangling inline link, an
unregistered role, a field out of order -- is not repeated here. Its
findings are also embedded in the payload so the page lists them.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
These are semantic-layer rules in a script (DEC-LAYER-STACK). They are allowed there for now on the operator's ruling that validation need not be modelled on joints yet, provided each is INDEXED -- which NAR-WHITEBOARD-VIEW-RULES does, so the porting inventory is a screen of the view.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: DEC-NARRATIVE-IS-THE-VIEW-NODE
  ROLE: Governed_By
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-NOTHING-DEPENDS-ON-A-NARRATIVE
  ROLE: Guarantees
